	)
	(text_box "- 150 W output (12 V, 12.5 A) from a 40 - 51 V input\n\n- Discrete GaN half-bridge switching at 400 kHz, adjustable 300 - 500 kHz in firmware\n\n- Fully digital control on a TI C2000 microcontroller: open loop, voltage mode and average current mode\n\n- Hardware protection independent of the CPU: cycle-by-cycle overcurrent, output and input overvoltage\n\n- Watchdog/enable gating; PWM overlap protection TBD\n\n- Input and output current, voltage and FET temperature sensing\n\n- Runs from the 48 V bus or an external 5 V bench supply for safe low-voltage bring-up\n\n- USB serial telemetry and JTAG debug\n\n- Reverse-polarity, fuse and TVS protection on the input"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18.415 22.6313 0)
		(size 67.945 66.9037)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
